BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unsung Ithacans: Downtown Walking Tour
DTSTART:20260918T213000Z
DTEND:20260918T224500Z
DTSTAMP:20260914T155238Z
UID:c6b49dc1c04a5f39ba73981928e9054ab0c63eda@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:History & Heritage
DESCRIPTION:Event by The History Center in Tompkins County\n110 North Tiog
 a Street within the Tompkins Center for History & Culture\, Ithaca\, NY\nP
 ublic\nIthaca's history isn't only written by the people whose names ended
  up on buildings. Unsung Ithacans is a new walking tour from The History C
 enter in Tompkins County that starts and ends at 110 North Tioga Street\, 
 winding through The Commons\, down State Street\, and into DeWitt Park to 
 visit the people who quietly shaped this city.\nYou'll meet a Greek immigr
 ant whose candy shop perfumed an entire block\, a husband-and-wife pair of
  doctors and scholars who desegregated a hospital and a university\, a cit
 y missionary who founded a children's home\, a young woman who gave her un
 wanted suitors nicknames like "Expire\," a minister who talked her way int
 o a doctorate no German university would grant a woman\, and a bulldog who
  rode the train to Cornell football games and once got arrested.\nUsing hi
 storic photographs\, maps\, and firsthand newspaper accounts\, guides brin
 g these stories back to life at the very spots where they happened. Their 
 lives span the late 1700s through the modern day\, and together they show 
 how Ithaca got built\, created\, and cooked into the place it is now.\nTou
 rs are Thursday-Saturday at 5:30 PM\nWhat: 75 minute walking tour over sid
 ewalks\, gravel paths\, and grass - with a slight incline\nWhere: The Hist
 ory Center in Tompkins County\, 110 N Tioga St\, Ithaca NY 14850\nWho: Thi
 s tour is designed for ages 16-116\nWear Comfortable Shoes\, Bring an Umbr
 ella\, Jacket\, and Water Bottle\nWeather - this tour takes place rain or 
 shine! In case of severe weather\, we’ll determine cancellations by 10:3
 0 am the morning-of.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.ly/o9b
 0uzpj/event/78458779/20260910173000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78458779/20260910173000
END:VEVENT
