DESCRIPTION:Manhattan Short: A Global Film Festival\nJoin us on September 
 25\, 2026\, as we participate on the 29th Annual MANHATTAN SHORT Film Fest
 ival. From September 24 to October 4\, 2026\, over 100\,000 film lovers ac
 ross the world will unite in over 500 cities on six continents for one rea
 son…to view and vote on the Finalists’ Films in the 29th Annual MANHAT
 TAN SHORT Film Festival.\nHere in Corning\, we will show the finalists’ 
 films in two free screenings: one at 2:30 PM and one at 7:00 PM. Afterward
 s\, you will able to vote for your favorite shorts. We will have all the v
 oting rules and criteria at the event.\nThis FREE showing will run about 2
  hours and 45 minutes\, with a 10 minute intermission about halfway throug
 h. The directors of each film will have a 30 second spot on screen to intr
 oduce their film to you\, the audience.\nWe hope to see all of you film lo
 vers here for the show!\nDetails:\nDate: September 25\nTime: 2:30 pm - 5:3
 0 pm OR 7:00 pm – 10:00 pm\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.tim
 e.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78456261/20260925190000
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78456261/20260925190000
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Pomarium Drag Show- Hosted by Tilia Cordata
DTSTART:20260925T233000Z
DTEND:20260926T035959Z
DTSTAMP:20260914T155238Z
UID:8633e5d36fb3927809da75e86442ac25e8bf1702@corning-events
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Performing Arts,LGBTQ+
DESCRIPTION:Hangar Theatre’s In Flight Entertainment Series Presents:\nT
 he Pomarium\nDrag Show Hosted by Tilia Cordata\nFriday\, September 25 @ 7:
 30 pm\nTickets: $20 (seating is general admission for this performance)\nA
 n immersive drag spectacular inspired by the wild apple forests of Kazakhs
 tan—the birthplace of the modern apple.\nStep into the ancient orchard w
 here myth\, magic\, and drag first took root.\nThe Pomarium is an immersiv
 e drag spectacular inspired by the wild apple forests of Kazakhstan—the 
 birthplace of the modern apple (Malus sieversii)—where towering trees ha
 ve flourished for millions of years and legends have taken root alongside 
 them. From this primordial forest\, the humble apple began a journey that 
 would shape civilizations\, inspire folklore\, and become one of history
 ’s most enduring symbols.\nThroughout the evening\, performers will guid
 e you through a living orchard of stories\, drawing on myths and legends f
 rom around the world. Encounter the forbidden fruit of Eden\, the golden a
 pples of the Hesperides\, the Apple of Discord that sparked the Trojan War
 \, the enchanted isle of Avalon\, Snow White’s poisoned temptation\, and
  countless other tales where apples represent love\, temptation\, beauty\,
  immortality\, transformation\, and fate.\nBlending high-concept drag\, da
 zzling costumes\, music\, comedy\, and theatrical storytelling\, The Pomar
 ium celebrates the apple not simply as a fruit\, but as a cultural icon wh
 ose roots stretch from the forests of Central Asia to every corner of the 
 globe. Like the apple itself\, drag is an act of cultivation—grafted fro
 m history\, nourished by community\, and forever evolving into something u
 nexpected and beautiful.\nJoin us beneath the branches for a night where s
 cience meets folklore\, history blossoms into fantasy\, and every performa
 nce bears forbidden fruit.\n\nSource: FLXcalendar - https://calendar.time.
 ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78440338/20260925193000
GEO:42.457531;-76.515267
LOCATION:Hangar Theatre\, 801 Taughannock Boulevard\, Ithaca\, New York\, 
 14850\, United States
STATUS:CONFIRMED
URL:https://calendar.time.ly/o9b0uzpj/event/78440338/20260925193000
END:VEVENT
